ame um I was  already a freelancer at this point and  the production company was in  pinched and they said can you design a  set of style frames for us it has for a  huge cellular company at the time and I  panicked  I don't like I've know you want me to  design something well obviously the  creative director for the company he  recognized that I had a creative eye  based on the animation work I had done  for them and he trusted me enough and I  was up front with him I said hey man  I've never designed I don't know if I  can do this and he you know he really  pushed me he's like I believe in you I  know you can do this and he actually  gave me that confidence to just try it  so I designed these style frames and you  know deliver them to the client they  were ecstatic they picked my designs to  go with great but like I said it's it's  layering up these elements inside of  After Effects and just getting this this  I for what works visually what does and  what looks good what colors work well  together what typefaces work you know  all these things together that's what  taught me to be a better motion designer  so I would suggest you don't have to do  this if you're a power user in Photoshop  stick with Photoshop I mean you can  design amazing style frames but if  you're a little bit timid with Photoshop  and you want to explore After Effects  even more get in there and design inside  of After Effects so just to plug one of  my curriculums that I teach it's called  style craft and stock craft I actually  teach you how to design inside of After  Effects so that's one of the main things  I teach so that's what I got for you  today I would love to hear from you in  the comments if you are designing an  After Effects what's your take on that  because I know more and more motion  designers are moving towards designing  an After Effects until next time I'm  Cameron and this is motion science see  ya  [Music]  you
 

